From 352fa854d425b9255c0bb3f8e1c582db156476d8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Miroslav Mraz <miroslav.mraz@techmania.cz>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 16:56:31 +0200
Subject: [PATCH v1 2/2] media: qcom: camss: Follow the enabled link when
 finding the sensor

camss_find_sensor_pad() walks the pipeline from a CAMSS entity towards
the sensor, but at each hop it blindly takes pads[0] and its first
remote pad. media_pad_remote_pad_first() only returns the remote of an
enabled link, so this works for entities with a single sink pad but
breaks on an intermediate entity that has several sink pads of which
only one is enabled at a time - a video mux.

On the a52q the ultra-wide and macro cameras share CSIPHY3 behind a
video mux:

  [gc5035_macro] -> [1|video-mux|2] -> [0|csiphy3|1] -> csid0 -> vfe0

The ultra-wide sits on mux input 0, so pads[0] happens to resolve it
and streaming works. The macro sits on input 1: camss_find_sensor_pad()
still looks at the mux's pads[0] (input 0), whose link is disabled,
gets NULL from media_pad_remote_pad_first() and returns NULL.
camss_get_link_freq() then returns -ENODEV and csiphy_stream_on()
aborts with

  qcom-camss acb3000.isp: Cannot get CSI2 transmitter's link frequency

so VIDIOC_STREAMON fails with -EINVAL. The WARN splat printed on the
same stream-on just above that line is the "Unknown format" WARN(1) in
csiphy_get_bpp(): it is the only WARN reachable in csiphy_stream_on()
before the error and fires when the CSIPHY sink pad holds a format that
is not in its table on the mis-resolved input.

Resolve each hop through the enabled link instead, using
media_entity_remote_source_pad_unique(), which scans all of the
entity's sink pads and returns the single remote source reached over an
enabled link - the same helper the CSI-2 receiver drivers use for mux
inputs. For a single-sink-pad CAMSS entity the result is unchanged, so
plain sensor pipelines and mux input 0 behave exactly as before.

The s_stream pipeline walk in camss-video.c does not need the same
change: it already stops at the first non-CAMSS subdev (the mux),
handing everything upstream to the mux's own .s_stream(), so it never
has to choose between the mux's sink pads.

Signed-off-by: Miroslav Mraz <miroslav.mraz@techmania.cz>
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c | 16 ++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c
index 96ec66fa755d..bfe8076fc04b 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c
@@ -4604,12 +4604,16 @@ struct media_pad *camss_find_sensor_pad(struct media_entity *entity)
 	struct media_pad *pad;
 
 	while (1) {
-		pad = &entity->pads[0];
-		if (!(pad->flags & MEDIA_PAD_FL_SINK))
-			return NULL;
-
-		pad = media_pad_remote_pad_first(pad);
-		if (!pad || !is_media_entity_v4l2_subdev(pad->entity))
+		/*
+		 * Follow the enabled sink link rather than pads[0]: an
+		 * intermediate entity such as a video mux has several sink pads
+		 * and only the one for the selected input is enabled, so keying
+		 * on pads[0] would miss the active sensor (and return NULL for
+		 * any input other than the first). For an entity with a single
+		 * sink pad this resolves to the same pad as before.
+		 */
+		pad = media_entity_remote_source_pad_unique(entity);
+		if (IS_ERR(pad) || !is_media_entity_v4l2_subdev(pad->entity))
 			return NULL;
 
 		entity = pad->entity;
